{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Both of them shall die.</b> The man who lies with a married woman and the woman. Even though both are liable, the offense of the man is greater than the offense of the woman, and this is why Scripture needed to repeat 'the man who lies with the woman and the woman' — it hung the offense on the man who lies, and did not say 'and the woman who is lain with'; so explained the Ramban, of blessed memory. And the Sages, of blessed memory, expounded in the first chapter of Qiddushin: ״ומתו גם שניהם״ — when both are equal, that is, in liability to execution, to exclude the adult who lies with the minor, for she is not one subject to punishment. And further they expounded: ״גם שניהם״ — to include the offspring, as we say in Arakhin: a woman who goes forth to be executed — they do not wait for her until she gives birth; if she sat on the birth-stool, they wait for her until she gives birth, as Rabbi Abbahu said in the name of Rabbi Yohanan: ״גם שניהם״ — to include the offspring."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:50:25.441431719Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}